# Publish lab images to Docker Hub (`starciacademy/*`)

StarCi course demos use **Docker Hub** namespace **`starciacademy`** (see `.rules/contents/system-design.md`). Images must be **built from the Dockerfile directory** (build context), tagged with the canonical name, then **pushed** after **`docker login`** (interactive or CI token).

## Lesson 0 — `metrics-api`

From module repo checkout:

```powershell
docker build -t starciacademy/monitoring-and-observability-metrics-api:latest `
  "c:\Repositories\ac\starci-academy-backend\system-design-mastery-module-7-monitoring-and-observability\0-monitoring-and-observability\metrics-api"

docker push starciacademy/monitoring-and-observability-metrics-api:latest
```

On **Linux/macOS**:

```bash
docker build -t starciacademy/monitoring-and-observability-metrics-api:latest \
  path/to/system-design-mastery-module-7-monitoring-and-observability/0-monitoring-and-observability/metrics-api

docker push starciacademy/monitoring-and-observability-metrics-api:latest
```

**Compose:** `0-monitoring-and-observability/.docker/compose.yaml` references **`image: starciacademy/monitoring-and-observability-metrics-api:latest`** for service **`app`** — pull works without local build once pushed.

## Auth

- **`docker login`** (Docker Hub user with push rights to **`starciacademy`** org).
- Push fails with **401/403** until login or PAT is configured — do not embed secrets in repo; use env / credential helper.

## Other lesson Dockerfiles

Use the same pattern: **`docker build -t starciacademy/<image-name>:latest <context-dir>`** then **`docker push`**. Prefer naming **`monitoring-and-observability-<service>`** for this module unless an existing canonical name already exists on Hub.
